{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AtomicMass.MagicNumbersFromQ","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.MagicNumbersFromQ","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":27,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AtomicMass.Phi_signal_support","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.Phi_signal_support","kind":"theorem","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AtomicMass/MagicNumbersFromQ.lean#L288-L299","doc":"**The tabulation's support is exactly the magic set it recovers.**\nAt `K = 10` only `Z ∈ {8, 20, 28}` is given a non-zero value, so the\npositivity of the second difference at those `Z` is a property of\nwhich entries were tabulated, not of the Hecke computation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AtomicMass.magic_numbers_from_q_holds_at_every_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.magic_numbers_from_q_holds_at_every_q","kind":"theorem","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AtomicMass/MagicNumbersFromQ.lean#L279-L286","doc":"**The headline theorem holds at every `q`, not only at `q₀`.**\nPinning the substrate value in `magic_numbers_from_q` is\npresentational: the same statement is provable at `q = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AtomicMass.delta2_Phi_q_independent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.delta2_Phi_q_independent","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AtomicMass/MagicNumbersFromQ.lean#L271-L277","doc":"`delta2_Phi` inherits the `q`-independence of `Phi_signal`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AtomicMass.Phi_signal_q_independent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.Phi_signal_q_independent","kind":"theorem","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AtomicMass/MagicNumbersFromQ.lean#L265-L269","doc":"`Phi_signal` is independent of `q`: the tabulation branches only on\n`K` and `Z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AtomicMass.magic_numbers_from_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.magic_numbers_from_q","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AtomicMass/MagicNumbersFromQ.lean#L219-L237","doc":"**Magic numbers from `q`.** Each predicted magic number `Z` in\n`{8, 20, 28}` (the open-shell positions visible at the\nHecke truncation `K = 10`) has positive second-difference\nsignal `δ² Φ_K(Z; q₀) > 0` at the pinned substrate value.\n\n`Z = 2` is below the `K = 3` Hecke threshold and therefore not\ncovered by this `K = 10` second-difference test (it appears at\na lower truncation level). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:magic-numbers-from-q","label":"conj:magic-numbers-from-q","md":"quantum-observable-universe/observations/magic-numbers-from-q.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AtomicMass.mem_predictedMagicNumbers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.mem_predictedMagicNumbers","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AtomicMass/MagicNumbersFromQ.lean#L210-L215","doc":"Membership in the predicted-magic list. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AtomicMass.predictedMagicNumbers_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.predictedMagicNumbers_eq","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AtomicMass/MagicNumbersFromQ.lean#L205-L208","doc":"The predicted set is exactly `{2, 8, 20, 28}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AtomicMass.delta2_declining","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.delta2_declining","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AtomicMass/MagicNumbersFromQ.lean#L191-L201","doc":"**Declining-amplitude property** (manuscript Remark): the\nsecond-difference signal decreases monotonically along the\nmagic sequence `8 → 20 → 28`, reflecting the hierarchical\nHecke-level resolution of higher shells. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AtomicMass.delta2_Phi_at_28","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.delta2_Phi_at_28","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AtomicMass/MagicNumbersFromQ.lean#L183-L189","doc":"**Exact value of the Z=28 second difference.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AtomicMass.delta2_Phi_at_20","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.delta2_Phi_at_20","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AtomicMass/MagicNumbersFromQ.lean#L175-L181","doc":"**Exact value of the Z=20 second difference.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AtomicMass.delta2_Phi_at_8","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.delta2_Phi_at_8","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AtomicMass/MagicNumbersFromQ.lean#L167-L173","doc":"**Exact value of the Z=8 second difference.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AtomicMass.hoefsmit_witness_28","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.hoefsmit_witness_28","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AtomicMass/MagicNumbersFromQ.lean#L158-L165","doc":"**Hoefsmit witness at Z = 28.** From manuscript Table 1:\n`δ² Φ(28) = 4.4 > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AtomicMass.hoefsmit_witness_20","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.hoefsmit_witness_20","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AtomicMass/MagicNumbersFromQ.lean#L149-L156","doc":"**Hoefsmit witness at Z = 20.** From manuscript Table 1:\n`δ² Φ(20) = 20.4 > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AtomicMass.hoefsmit_witness_8","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.hoefsmit_witness_8","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AtomicMass/MagicNumbersFromQ.lean#L139-L147","doc":"**Hoefsmit witness at Z = 8.** From manuscript Table 1:\n`δ² Φ(8) = 33.2 > 0`. Now proved from the `Phi_signal`\ntabulation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AtomicMass.Phi_signal_at_26","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.Phi_signal_at_26","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AtomicMass/MagicNumbersFromQ.lean#L133-L135","doc":"`Phi_signal 10 26 q = 0` (off-table). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AtomicMass.Phi_signal_at_27","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.Phi_signal_at_27","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AtomicMass/MagicNumbersFromQ.lean#L129-L131","doc":"`Phi_signal 10 27 q = 0` (off-table). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AtomicMass.Phi_signal_at_28","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.Phi_signal_at_28","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AtomicMass/MagicNumbersFromQ.lean#L125-L127","doc":"`Phi_signal 10 28 q = 4.4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AtomicMass.Phi_signal_at_18","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.Phi_signal_at_18","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AtomicMass/MagicNumbersFromQ.lean#L121-L123","doc":"`Phi_signal 10 18 q = 0` (off-table). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AtomicMass.Phi_signal_at_19","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.Phi_signal_at_19","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AtomicMass/MagicNumbersFromQ.lean#L117-L119","doc":"`Phi_signal 10 19 q = 0` (off-table). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AtomicMass.Phi_signal_at_20","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.Phi_signal_at_20","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AtomicMass/MagicNumbersFromQ.lean#L113-L115","doc":"`Phi_signal 10 20 q = 20.4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AtomicMass.Phi_signal_at_6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.Phi_signal_at_6","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AtomicMass/MagicNumbersFromQ.lean#L109-L111","doc":"`Phi_signal 10 6 q = 0` (off-table). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AtomicMass.Phi_signal_at_7","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.Phi_signal_at_7","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AtomicMass/MagicNumbersFromQ.lean#L105-L107","doc":"`Phi_signal 10 7 q = 0` (off-table). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AtomicMass.Phi_signal_at_8","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.Phi_signal_at_8","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AtomicMass/MagicNumbersFromQ.lean#L101-L103","doc":"`Phi_signal 10 8 q = 33.2` for any `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AtomicMass.predictedMagicNumbers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.predictedMagicNumbers","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AtomicMass/MagicNumbersFromQ.lean#L93-L97","doc":"The nuclear magic numbers predicted by the framework at the\nHecke truncation `K = 10`. These are the elements of\n`{2, 8, 20, 28}` — the open-shell positions where the Hoefsmit\nsecond-difference signal peaks per manuscript Table 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AtomicMass.delta2_Phi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.delta2_Phi","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AtomicMass/MagicNumbersFromQ.lean#L87-L89","doc":"Forward second difference `δ² Φ(Z) = Φ(Z) − 2Φ(Z−1) + Φ(Z−2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AtomicMass.Phi_signal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.Phi_signal","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AtomicMass/MagicNumbersFromQ.lean#L81-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AtomicMass.q_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AtomicMass.q_zero","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AtomicMass/MagicNumbersFromQ.lean#L52-L58","doc":"Pinned substrate parameter `q₀ ≈ 1.1097`. The 4-digit decimal\nis the same value used throughout the manuscript\n(`MassDerivation.substrate_q`); the unified 50-digit witness\nlives in `q-pinning` and tightens this without changing the\n`Phi_signal` tabulation, which branches only on `K` and `Z`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}